  "companyID": "58c62e995865713647a7115d",
  "created": "2018-08-30T20:36:16.229Z",
  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "Currently the player's voice comes out of where the head bone is located. For puppet type models that move around via the hands and have a fake armature or other odd shaped avatar, the voice will come out of thin air nowhere near the mouth. It would be handy if there was a value in the avatar descriptor that would allow manually setting a bone for where your voice comes out of.  It would add a nice extra layer to some models",
